<article>
    <h1 id="top">Welcome to a website about GNU/Linux!</h1>
    <hr>
    <p>If you're here, that means that you've shown some interest in alternative operating systems for your computer. The path ahead, I will immediately warn you, is not entirely simple or worry-free. But it will be liberating to walk through, and you can stop at any point. The purpose of this website is to try to help you through it as much as I can.</p>
    <p>In an age of corporate rulers, where computers feel like they use you more than you use them, where LLMs are invading and taking over everything you love, where your personal privacy is being violated without your consent more times than you can count every single day, where you are only ever annoyed or outright scared every time your OS updates, where every "innovation" is only so insofar as it is an innovative way to extract money from you... There is another way.</p>
    <p>This website is a very surface-level view about a subject as deep as the Mariana's trench. I will cover only what I think is the minimum amount of things that concern you and I will do my best to explain them without any technical jargon.</p>
    <p>I have an obviously biased perspective, but I do not consider myself an evangelist - I will not hide the pain points of using GNU/Linux or its many problems. Whether they are dwarfed by those of MacOS or Windows in comparison or not is your judgement to make.</p>
    <p>This website is meant to be read in top-to-bottom order, but feel free to skip around. If you're ready to start, your journey begins at <a href="./why.html">Why use GNU/Linux?</a>.</p>

